course: dictionary
lesson: 7410
title: One word, many meanings: poison
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Poison can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, a poison is a substance that can make you very ill or kill you. As a verb, to poison means to harm or kill someone with poison, or to put poison in something. The verb changes: poisons, poisoned, poisoning.
explain: Look at the words around poison to find its meaning. «Taking more of a medicine than the dose on the label can poison you» uses poison as a verb: the medicine does the harm. Words like rat, food and ivy tell you what kind of poison it is.
explain: Poison can also mean something that spoils or harms, even when it is not a real substance. «Gossip is poison to a friendship» means gossip harms a friendship. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: Poison is serious, so remember this safety rule. Many things at home are poisons, such as bleach, cleaning sprays, medicines and button batteries. Keep them in their containers, locked away from small children, and look for the warning symbols.
fact: Poison (noun) means a substance that can make you very ill or kill you if you swallow it, breathe it in or touch it.
fact: Poison (verb) means to harm or kill someone with poison, or to put poison in something.
fact: «Gossip is poison to a friendship» uses poison to mean something that spoils or harms.
fact: If someone swallows poison, tell an adult at once and call the poison help line or emergency number. Do not make them sick.
fact: Some animals use venom, and some plants and mushrooms are poisonous, which means they can harm you if you eat or touch them.
exercise: «Taking more of a medicine than the dose on the label can poison you.» In this sentence, what kind of word is poison? | A noun, a kind of plant | *A verb, an action that harms you | A noun, a kind of medicine | A noun, a kind of sweet
exercise: «Gossip is poison to a friendship.» What does poison mean here? | A kind of drink | *Something that spoils or harms | A green plant
exercise: Someone has swallowed poison. What should you do first? | Give them more food | Make them sick to get it out | *Tell an adult at once and call the poison help line or emergency number | Wait and see if they feel better
test: «Fish should get only as much food as they eat in a couple of minutes, because leftovers rot and poison the water.» What does poison mean here? | To cool something down | To cook something | *To harm or spoil something | To catch something
test: «Never use a stove, heater or barbecue inside a tent, because of carbon monoxide, a poison gas you cannot smell.» What is poison describing? | *A harmful gas you cannot smell | A type of barbecue | A type of tent | A pleasant smell from a stove
exam: In the story of Snow White, what does «poisoned» mean in «the poisoned apple»? | Cooked in a pie | Shiny and red | Bitten by a dog | *Filled with a substance that can harm or kill
